claim.claim-text:
receiving (504) a command at a host interface (304);
distributing the command among a first set of data paths (336A-D),
wherein each data path in the first set of data paths (336A-D) have substantially a first bandwidth;
multiplexing the command onto one network port (328A, 436A) when the command requires more than the first bandwidth; and
transmitting the command via the one network port (328A, 436A).

receiving (604) a frame at a network port (348A-D);
utilizing a de-multiplexer (352, 448) to assign and mark a serial number onto a beginning of the frame;
de-multiplexing the frame with the de-multiplexer (352, 448) to create a de-multiplexed frame;
distributing (616) the de-multiplexed frame among a set of receive data paths (356A-D), wherein each data path in the set of data paths (356A-D) comprises a bandwidth that is less than a bandwidth of the network port (348A-D; 452A-D);
re-ordering (616) the de-multiplexed frame at an egress of the set of receive data paths (356A-D); and
providing (628) the re-ordered frame to a host interface (304, 404).
